---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import { METHODOLOGY } from '../data/methodology';import '../styles/content-pages.css';
const revised=new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US',{dateStyle:'long',timeZone:'UTC'}).format(new Date(`${METHODOLOGY.revisionDate}T00:00:00Z`));
---
<Layout title="Benchmark Revisions | Ultimate Bench" description="Current Ultimate Bench methodology version, revision date, normalization migration note, and versioning policy."><main class="content-page"><header class="page-heading"><span class="page-kicker">Public audit trail</span><h1>Benchmark revisions</h1><p>Version and comparability notes for the currently published methodology and dataset.</p></header><article class="content-card"><h2>Current publication</h2><p><strong>Methodology version:</strong> {METHODOLOGY.version}<br/><strong>Revision date:</strong> {revised}</p><h2>29 July 2026 · fixed six-level normalization</h2><p>Every arena moved to the permanent six-level denominator 63, with Planned and Locked weights reserved. Hydra returned from Active to Locked because no model had passed Python, and prior Hydra model results were removed. Visual, Data Retrieval, Chess, and Overall scores changed; former active-only-denominator scores are not directly comparable.</p><p>The methodology was revised on 30 July 2026 to state that every Active level is administered independently, so zero or INVALID at one level never prevents a later Active-level administration.</p><h2>Version treatment</h2><p>Material changes to scoring, qualification, or comparability receive explicit methodology-version treatment and a revision entry. Ordinary site releases do not silently change the methodology version.</p><p><a href={METHODOLOGY.overviewPath}>Read the current methodology</a> · <a href="https://github.com/ame-888/ultimate-bench">Inspect the GitHub repository</a></p></article></main></Layout>
